  "description": "Loft conversion with dormers, solar panels and AC unit ",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-b88aed46-7fff-287a-5411-4a17a771a4f5&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;It is considered that the applicant has failed to adhere to the cooling hierarchy&amp;nbsp; and no details on passive overheating mitigations have been considered. Therefore, it is considered that the proposed development would be contrary to LP33 policy LP55 (Mitigating Climate Change) and policies Sl2 (Minimising Greenhouse Gas Emissions) and Sl4 (Managing Heat Risk) of The London Plan and the proposal should be refused.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span id=&quot;docs-internal-guid-1880736b-7fff-1ef2-d192-ace3808f6c83&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap;&quot;&gt;The proposed development would, by reason of scale, siting, detailed design, and massing, be an incongruous and unsympathetic addition to the host building, resulting in the disruption of an original roof line, detrimental to the character and appearance of the site, the wider terrace and the street scene of Palatine Road (including nearby adjoining roads). Therefore, it is considered that the proposed development would be contrary to LP33 policy LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character) and policy D4 (Delivering good design) of The London Plan.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
